<title>USA: Berkshire Realty Co Q4 full results.</title>
<headline>Berkshire Realty Co Q4 full results.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in thousands)</p>
<p>	Quarter Ended December 31,	Year Ended December 31,</p>
<p>		 1996    1995  % Change   1996     1995  % Change</p>
<p> Revenues   $12,108 $11,819   2.45%  $48,499  $45,566   6.44%</p>
<p> Expenses     5,843   5,817   0.45%   23,042   22,197   3.81%</p>
<p>Net operating</p>
<p>   income     6,265   6,002   4.38%   25,457   23,369   8.93%</p>
<p>Average</p>
<p>   occupancy    94%     96%	--	95%	93%	--</p>
<p>Average monthly</p>
<p>rent per unit</p>
<p>		    640     620	--	632	608	--</p>
<p>Growth in same-store multi-family revenues was approximately 6.4% for 1996 when compared to 1995.  Rent increases accounted for 4.3% of the increase and higher occupancies contributed to the remaining 2.4%. Occupancy at December 31, 1996 was 93.5% for same-store assets.  Occupancies for the total multi-family portfolio, including recently acquired assets in their value- enhancement stage, was 93% at December 31, 1996.</p>
